Package: panero
Architecture: any
# kio/kinit: KIO workers (kioslave5, file, trash, ...) and klauncher, needed
#   for every file operation; mirrors the Ubuntu krusader package.
# ktexteditor-katepart: the internal editor (F4) is the Kate text editor part;
#   without it Panero warns on first start and cannot edit files.
# breeze-icon-theme: Panero uses KDE icon names and falls back to Breeze; on
#   non-KDE desktops (Zorin/GNOME) toolbars and menus lose most icons without it.
Depends: breeze-icon-theme,
         kinit,
         kio,
         ktexteditor-katepart,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
# kio-extras: sftp/smb/fish/man/... protocols and the basic thumbnailers;
# kdegraphics-thumbnailers, ffmpegthumbs, kimageformat-plugins: PDF/RAW, video
#   and extra image format previews (same set the Ubuntu dolphin package recommends);
# packagekit: Panero offers to install KDiff3 through PackageKit's D-Bus
#   service (authorised by the desktop's polkit agent) when it is missing.
Recommends: ffmpegthumbs,
            kdegraphics-thumbnailers,
            kimageformat-plugins,
            kio-extras,
            packagekit,
# Optional helpers detected at runtime (mirrors the Ubuntu krusader package's
# Suggests with noble package names). KDiff3 stays optional by design: when
# it is missing, Panero offers to install it through PackageKit.
# qt5-gtk-platformtheme: GTK file dialogs/fonts on GNOME-based desktops when
#   Panero's own look (Fusion style, built into Qt) is switched off.
# kde-cli-tools: kdesu for "Start Root Mode Panero" and root user actions. Only
#   suggested: it recommends systemsettings, which would add a "KDE System
#   Settings" launcher to a GNOME/Zorin desktop (see D-011). Panero explains what to
#   install if root mode is started without it.
Suggests: 7zip,
          arj,
          ark,
          bzip2,
          cpio,
          hashdeep,
          kate,
          kde-cli-tools,
          kdiff3,
          kompare | xxdiff,
          konsole,
          krename,
          lhasa,
          okteta,
          qt5-gtk-platformtheme,
          rpm,
          unace,
          unrar | unrar-free | rar,
          unzip,
          zip,
Description: twin-panel (commander-style) file manager based on Krusader
 Panero is a native twin-panel file manager for Linux with a workflow familiar
 to Total Commander and Midnight Commander users. It keeps the file-management
 engine of Krusader: tabbed panels, keyboard-driven operation, advanced
 search, a directory synchronizer, folder comparison, disk usage analysis,
 a built-in viewer and editor, user actions, bookmarks, and transparent
 handling of archives and remote locations through KIO.
 .
 Panero is an independent fork of Krusader. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by KDE or the Krusader maintainers.
 .
 The package installs next to the krusader package without sharing files or
 settings; Panero keeps its configuration in ~/.config/panerorc and
 ~/.local/share/panero.
